// ---- Glow waves ------------------------------------------------------------
//
// THE AXIS A GLOW NEVER HAD. A glow varies per pixel going UP a wall and was
// one flat value going ALONG it, because reach arrives as a single number for
// the whole surface. Beautiful fade top to bottom, dead straight top edge from
// one end of the room to the other.
//
// This is a world-space wave that moves the reach per fragment, so the edge
// itself rises and falls. It can drive brightness and the two-colour boundary
// as well -- one wave read into three terms that look nothing like each other.
//
// EXCLUSIVE WITH SEAMLESS CORNERS, on purpose. The corner works by matching
// reach across the junction; undulate one side and every corner grows a moving
// seam. Either the room is bounded by continuous colour with no edge anywhere,
// or it is bounded by an edge that moves. Those are two different rooms.
server bool gitd_wave_enabled = false;

